   <div class=3D"example" id=3D"example-throwifaborted">
    <a class=3D"self-link" href=3D"https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#example-thr=
owifaborted"></a>
=20
    <p>This method is primarily useful for when functions accepting <code c=
lass=3D"idl"><a data-link-type=3D"idl" href=3D"https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/=
#abortsignal" id=3D"ref-for-abortsignal=E2=91=A2=E2=91=A3">AbortSignal</a><=
/code>s want to throw (or
 return a rejected promise) at specific checkpoints, instead of passing alo=
ng the <code class=3D"idl"><a data-link-type=3D"idl" href=3D"https://dom.sp=
ec.whatwg.org/#abortsignal" id=3D"ref-for-abortsignal=E2=91=A2=E2=91=A4">Ab=
ortSignal</a></code>
 to other methods. For example, the following function allows aborting in b=
etween each attempt to
 poll for a condition. This gives opportunities to abort the polling proces=
s, even though the
 actual asynchronous operation (i.e., <code class=3D"highlight lang-javascr=
ipt"><c- k=3D"">await</c-> func<c- p=3D"">()</c-></code>) does not
 accept an <code class=3D"idl"><a data-link-type=3D"idl" href=3D"https://do=
