   <div class=3D"algorithm" data-algorithm=3D"cloning steps">
   =20
<a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#other-applic=
able-specifications" id=3D"ref-for-other-applicable-specifications=E2=91=A5=
">Specifications</a> may define
<dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-type=3D"dfn" data-export=3D"" id=3D"con=
cept-node-clone-ext">cloning steps</dfn> for all or some <a data-link-type=
=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-node" id=3D"ref-for-c=
oncept-node=E2=91=A0=E2=91=A2=E2=93=AA">nodes</a>. The
algorithm is passed <var>node</var>, <var>copy</var>, and <var>subtree</var=
> as
indicated in the <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://dom.spec.whatwg.=
org/#concept-node-clone" id=3D"ref-for-concept-node-clone">clone a node</a>=
 algorithm.


    <p class=3D"note" role=3D"note">HTML defines <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" =
href=3D"https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-node-clone-ext" id=3D"ref-for-=
concept-node-clone-ext">cloning steps</a> for several elements, such as <co=
de><a data-link-type=3D"element" href=3D"https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multi=
page/input.html#the-input-element" id=3D"ref-for-the-input-element=E2=91=A0=
">input</a></code>, <code><a data-link-type=3D"element" href=3D"https://htm=
l.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/scripting.html#script" id=3D"ref-for-script=E2=
=91=A2">script</a></code>,
and <code><a data-link-type=3D"element" href=3D"https://html.spec.whatwg.or=
g/multipage/scripting.html#the-template-element" id=3D"ref-for-the-template=
-element">template</a></code>. SVG ought to do the same for its <code><a da=
ta-link-type=3D"element" href=3D"https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/scr=
ipting.html#script" id=3D"ref-for-script=E2=91=A3">script</a></code> elemen=
ts, but does not.
</p>
