   <hr>
   <p>An <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#con=
cept-element" id=3D"ref-for-concept-element=E2=91=A8=E2=91=A0">element</a> =
can have an associated
<dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-for=3D"Element" data-dfn-type=3D"dfn" d=
ata-export=3D"" data-lt=3D"ID" id=3D"concept-id">unique identifier (ID)</df=
n>

</p>
   <p class=3D"note" role=3D"note">Historically <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" h=
ref=3D"https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-element" id=3D"ref-for-concept-=
element=E2=91=A8=E2=91=A1">elements</a> could have multiple identifiers e.g=
., by using
the HTML <code>id</code> <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://dom.spec=
.whatwg.org/#concept-attribute" id=3D"ref-for-concept-attribute=E2=91=A2=E2=
=91=A0">attribute</a> and a DTD. This specification makes <a data-link-type=
=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-id" id=3D"ref-for-con=
cept-id=E2=91=A5">ID</a>
a concept of the DOM and allows for only one per <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" =
href=3D"https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-element" id=3D"ref-for-concept=
-element=E2=91=A8=E2=91=A2">element</a>, given by an
<a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-name=
d-attribute" id=3D"ref-for-concept-named-attribute=E2=91=A2"><code>id</code=
> attribute</a>.

</p>
   <p>Use these <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://dom.spec.whatwg.o=
rg/#concept-element-attributes-change-ext" id=3D"ref-for-concept-element-at=
tributes-change-ext=E2=91=A2">attribute change steps</a> to update an <a da=
ta-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-element" =
id=3D"ref-for-concept-element=E2=91=A8=E2=91=A3">element</a>=E2=80=99s
<a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-id" =
id=3D"ref-for-concept-id=E2=91=A6">ID</a>:

</p>
   <ol>
    <li>
     <p>If <var>localName</var> is <code>id</code>, <var>namespace</var> is=
 null, and
 <var>value</var> is null or the empty string, then unset <var>element</var=
>=E2=80=99s
 <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-id"=
 id=3D"ref-for-concept-id=E2=91=A7">ID</a>.

 </p>
    </li><li>
     <p>Otherwise, if <var>localName</var> is <code>id</code>, <var>namespa=
ce</var> is null, then
 set <var>element</var>=E2=80=99s <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https:/=
/dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-id" id=3D"ref-for-concept-id=E2=91=A8">ID</a>=
 to <var>value</var>.
</p>
   </li></ol>
   <p class=3D"note" role=3D"note">While this specification defines require=
ments for <code>class</code>,
<code>id</code>, and <code>slot</code> <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"ht=
tps://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-attribute" id=3D"ref-for-concept-attribu=
te=E2=91=A2=E2=91=A1">attributes</a> on any <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=
=3D"https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-element" id=3D"ref-for-concept-ele=
ment=E2=91=A8=E2=91=A4">element</a>, it makes no
claims as to whether using them is conforming or not.

</p>
   <hr>
   <p>A <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#conc=
ept-node" id=3D"ref-for-concept-node=E2=91=A0=E2=91=A5=E2=91=A2">node</a>=
=E2=80=99s <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#c=
oncept-tree-parent" id=3D"ref-for-concept-tree-parent=E2=91=A2=E2=91=A1">pa=
rent</a> of type <code class=3D"idl"><a data-link-type=3D"idl" href=3D"http=
s://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#element" id=3D"ref-for-element=E2=91=A3=E2=91=A8">=
Element</a></code> is known as its
<dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-type=3D"dfn" data-export=3D"" id=3D"par=
ent-element">parent element</dfn>. If the <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D=
"https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-node" id=3D"ref-for-concept-node=E2=
=91=A0=E2=91=A5=E2=91=A3">node</a> has a
<a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-tree=
